{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f","name":"Noble","source":{"id":"source:reference-190d375ec3483f8f","title":"Noble","revision":18386,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:03:13Z","sha256":"29ef96aaa8a7008d3843c009d9ca0ceb25e1ee0860f9988abcf11c2d78bf7e35","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18386","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Noble&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-190d375ec3483f8f","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Nobles use their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"}," and natural ",{"tag":"a","children":["Charisma"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Charisma"}," to make their way in the galaxy. From true royalty to elected officials, military commanders to crime lords, traders, merchants, ambassadors, Holovid stars, and influential corporate magnates, character types who appear in the Noble class are varied and numerous. Some bring honor to the name. Others are sly, treacherous, and dishonorable to the core. With a winning smile, golden tongue, a powerful message, or a knack for making compromises, the Noble commands respect, makes friends, and inevitably influences people.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Adventurers"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Most Nobles wind up in dangerous situations because of something they believe in or because their job calls for it. Others hope to use their negotiating talents to navigate a course through the troubles around them, or seek to find profit in the troubles of others. Whatever their initial motivations, Nobles usually wind up taking to a cause and a goal that sustains them through the roughest missions. An adventuring Noble might be a senator's aide, a free trader, a diplomat, a true prince or princess, or an outlaw's lieutenant. Nobles often feel responsible for others, though some consider themselves to be better than those around them.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Characteristics"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The Noble fosters feelings of good will and honesty, or at least the illusion of such, to succeed. Where other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heroic Classes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heroic_Classes","referenceId":"reference:3db50eedfbef40fc"}," shoot first, the Noble starts out asking questions and hopes to finish by negotiating a deal. The Noble believes he or she can be more effective with words and deeds than with violence, though some draw a blaster when push comes to shove. The Noble is more comfortable in civilized regions of space, where law and order have some meaning. Of all the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heroic Classes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heroic_Classes","referenceId":"reference:3db50eedfbef40fc"},", Nobles have the best diplomatic and bargaining skills. They're good talkers, negotiators, and bluffers. They have a knack for inspiring others, and they make good leaders.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Backgrounds"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Nobles come to their profession in a variety of ways. Altruistic Nobles believe it is their duty and responsibility to serve and lead. More selfish Nobles seek the fame, wealth, and power often associated with the position they aspire to. Power-hungry Nobles take advantages of the system and wind up helping others only to help themselves. The halls of power are calling. How the Noble answers can make all the difference.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Examples of Nobles in Star Wars"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Leia Organa, Padmé Amidala, Bail Organa, Talon Karrde, Jabba the Hutt, Chancellor Valorum, Supreme Chancellor Palpatine\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Game Rule Information"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Nobles have the following game statistics:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CLASS LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["BASE ATTACK BONUS"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/BASE_ATTACK_BONUS"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CLASS FEATURES\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["\n"],"rowspan":11},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CLASS LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["BASE ATTACK BONUS"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/BASE_ATTACK_BONUS"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CLASS FEATURES\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+0\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Defense"}," Bonuses, Starting ",{"tag":"a","children":["Feats"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Feats","referenceId":"reference:9194ccf56b9cace0"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble Talent"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble_Talent"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["11\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+8\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Noble Talent"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble_Talent"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+1\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Noble Bonus Feat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble_Bonus_Feat"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["12\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+9\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Noble Bonus Feat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble_Bonus_Feat"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["3\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+2\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Noble Talent"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble_Talent"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["13\n"]},"\n"